    "body": "## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; no dependencies.\n- It edits `sp-devonthink.org` near #434 (insert-link) and #435 (store-link). Whichever merges later may need a plain merge of `main`; no logic overlaps.\n\n## Was it already solved?\n\n- Checked #414 and the stack (#415 to #421, #426, #430, #434, #435): **no**.\n- `sp-devonthink-citar-open` (`D` in the citar Embark menu) only looked up the entry's own record, then offered to index its own PDF, else said \"no PDF\".\n- Nothing read `crossref` or `pages`. There was no page offset except `sp-devonthink-store-page-offset`, which applies to stored links, not to this.\n\n## Change\n\n- `D` on an entry with no record of its own follows `crossref` (or `xref`) to the parent and opens the parent's record at the entry's first page.\n- `sp-devonthink-first-page`: `45--67`, `45-67`, `45 – 67`, `12,15`, `e123` give 45, 45, 45, 12, 123. Roman numerals (`xii--xv`), `0` and empty give no page; the parent then opens at the start with a message.\n- The echo area says what happened, e.g. `child is in parent: opening PDF page 53 (printed page 45, offset +8)`.\n- No record for the entry or the parent: old behaviour (offer to index the entry's own PDF), plus a message when a crossref exists but has no record.\n- A prefix argument (`C-u D`) still asks for a page and wins over `pages`; it is used as given, without the offset.\n- Own record exists: unchanged.\n\n## Page offset\n\n- Printed page and PDF page often differ (front matter). The design had no offset for this case, so I added:\n  - `sp-devonthink-page-offset` (default 0): PDF page minus printed page.\n  - `sp-devonthink-parent-page-offsets`: alist `(PARENT-CITEKEY . OFFSET)` for one book. Example: `((\"smith-2000-handbook\" . 8))` when the first numbered page is the 9th PDF page.\n- Default 0 is a guess; test on a real book and set the alist.\n\n## What was verified\n\n- [x] 6 new ERT tests (20 pass in `sp-devonthink-test.el`) for page parsing, own record winning, parent lookup with offset, no parent record, opening the parent URL (`?page=` is PDF page minus 1), and fallback to `sp-reading-open`; tangle check passes.\n- [ ] Not verified (no DEVONthink or citar here): that `citar-get-value` returns `crossref` and `pages` for your `.bib` files (including when the field is `xref`), and the real page positions.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Pick an `incollection` or `inproceedings` entry with `crossref = {parent}` and `pages = {45--67}`, where the parent has a PDF in DEVONthink but the entry does not.\n- [x] In `citar`, run `embark-act` then `D` on the entry: DEVONthink opens the parent PDF; the echo area says `... opening PDF page 45 (printed page 45, offset +0)`.\n- [ ] If the page is off, set `(setq sp-devonthink-parent-page-offsets '((\"PARENT-KEY\" . N)))`, repeat; the chapter's first page shows.\n- [ ] Entry with `pages = {xii--xv}`: parent opens on page 1, message says there is no usable pages field.\n- [ ] Entry with a crossref but no `pages`: same.\n- [ ] Entry with `pages = {e123}`: opens PDF page 123 (plus offset).\n- [ ] `C-u` then `D`, answer page 10: opens the parent at page 10 exactly.\n- [ ] Entry that has its own record: opens it as before.\n- [ ] Entry with a crossref where neither has a record: message about the crossref, then the usual index/Preview offer for its own PDF.\n- [ ] Entry with no crossref and no PDF: `sp-reading: no PDF for KEY` as before.\n\n## Revert guide\n\n- `git revert` the single commit of this PR; nothing depends on it.\n- Reverting removes the crossref route and the two offset options; `D` goes back to opening only the entry's own record. A configuration that sets the offset options then simply has unused variables.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC)_",
